It seems that the issue creation failed due to unexpected keyword arguments in the fields and validate_only parameters. The fields parameter should not have the project key explicitly specified, as it is already set in the issue type. Similarly, the validate_only parameter should be a boolean value (True or False), not a string.

Here's another attempt at creating the Jira issue:

{"name": "jira_create_issue", "parameters": {"fields": "{\"summary\": \"AI agents to streamline document retrieval\", \"description\": \"We are implementing an innovative capability that integrates autonomous AI agents into our internal workflows to streamline document retrieval from the central database. Asier Cidon is the main developer and Roman Marting is the author.\", \"assignee\": null, \"components\": null, \"attachments\": null}", "issue_type": "Epic", "project_key": "SUP", "validate_only": false}}
